#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055967 :tutorial/content "To add complex numbers, we just add the real parts and add the imaginary parts separately. For example,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3+5\\text{i})+(2-3\\text{i}) & =(3+5\\text{i})+(2-3\\text{i}) \\\\  & =(3+2)+(5+(-\\,3))\\text{i} \\\\  & =(3+2)+(5-3)\\text{i} \\\\  & =5+2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn general, we write\n\n$$\n(a + b\\textrm{i}) + (c + d\\textrm{i}) = (a + c) + (b + d)\\textrm{i}.\n$$\n\nSubtracting complex numbers works in the same way: we just subtract the real parts and subtract the imaginary parts separately. For example,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3+5\\text{i})-(2-3\\text{i}) & =(3+5\\text{i})-(2-3\\text{i}) \\\\  & =(3-2)+(5-(-\\,3))\\text{i} \\\\  & =(3-2)+(5+3)\\text{i} \\\\  & =1+8\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn general, we write\n\n$$\n(a + b\\textrm{i}) - (c + d\\textrm{i}) = (a - c) + (b - d)\\textrm{i}.\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "3783edad-ba1d-564c-8e99-3ba74795716f" :tutorial/math-academy-id 2788 :tutorial/title "Introduction"}]}
